steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1785071190
      nanos: 336762389
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Act as an expert full-stack developer and system architect. I want you to build a complete, production-ready Next.js (App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS) web application that functions as a personal YouTube Music clone. \n\n### Critical Architecture Rules:\n- **No Database:** Do not use PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or any external database. Since I am the only user, store custom playlists, liked tracks, and local library metadata in a simple local JSON file (e.g., `data/playlists.json`) managed via Node.js file system (`fs`) calls.\n- **Single-User Security:** Use NextAuth.js with Google OAuth, but hardcode an email check so that **only my specific email address** (`YOUR_EMAIL@gmail.com`) can successfully authenticate and access the app. Block all other users.\n- **Styling:** Use Tailwind CSS to design a dark-themed UI matching YouTube Music (sidebar navigation, main content grid, and a sticky bottom audio player).\n\n### Detailed Component & Feature Requirements:\n\n1. **Authentication (NextAuth.js + Google):**\n   - Configure Google provider.\n   - Add a callback/session check to ensure the logged-in user\'s email matches your authorized email, redirecting unauthorized users to an error or login page.\n\n2. **yt-dlp Backend Audio Stream Extraction:**\n   - Create a Next.js API route (or a lightweight Node child-process wrapper) that executes `yt-dlp` to fetch direct audio stream URLs and metadata (title, thumbnail, duration) dynamically on the fly.\n   - Use the necessary client spoofing flags (`--extractor-args \"youtube:player_client=android,web\"`) to prevent bot blocks and `AudioProviderError`.\n\n3. **Core Features & UI:**\n   - **Search & Add:** An input field to paste a YouTube/YouTube Music URL or search query, which fetches track details via `yt-dlp` and saves it into the local `playlists.json` file.\n   - **Dashboard/Library:** Displays the saved tracks loaded from the local JSON file.\n   - **Sticky Bottom Player:** A functional HTML5 audio player bar with play/pause, seek bar, current track metadata, and thumbnail.\n\n### Deliverables Required:\n- The full project structure and file tree.\n- `package.json` with required dependencies.\n- The NextAuth configuration file with the strict email check.\n- The `yt-dlp` API route handler.\n- Core TSX components (Layout, Sidebar, Dashboard, and Sticky Player)."
    items {
      text: "Act as an expert full-stack developer and system architect. I want you to build a complete, production-ready Next.js (App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS) web application that functions as a personal YouTube Music clone. \n\n### Critical Architecture Rules:\n- **No Database:** Do not use PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or any external database. Since I am the only user, store custom playlists, liked tracks, and local library metadata in a simple local JSON file (e.g., `data/playlists.json`) managed via Node.js file system (`fs`) calls.\n- **Single-User Security:** Use NextAuth.js with Google OAuth, but hardcode an email check so that **only my specific email address** (`YOUR_EMAIL@gmail.com`) can successfully authenticate and access the app. Block all other users.\n- **Styling:** Use Tailwind CSS to design a dark-themed UI matching YouTube Music (sidebar navigation, main content grid, and a sticky bottom audio player).\n\n### Detailed Component & Feature Requirements:\n\n1. **Authentication (NextAuth.js + Google):**\n   - Configure Google provider.\n   - Add a callback/session check to ensure the logged-in user\'s email matches your authorized email, redirecting unauthorized users to an error or login page.\n\n2. **yt-dlp Backend Audio Stream Extraction:**\n   - Create a Next.js API route (or a lightweight Node child-process wrapper) that executes `yt-dlp` to fetch direct audio stream URLs and metadata (title, thumbnail, duration) dynamically on the fly.\n   - Use the necessary client spoofing flags (`--extractor-args \"youtube:player_client=android,web\"`) to prevent bot blocks and `AudioProviderError`.\n\n3. **Core Features & UI:**\n   - **Search & Add:** An input field to paste a YouTube/YouTube Music URL or search query, which fetches track details via `yt-dlp` and saves it into the local `playlists.json` file.\n   - **Dashboard/Library:** Displays the saved tracks loaded from the local JSON file.\n   - **Sticky Bottom Player:** A functional HTML5 audio player bar with play/pause, seek bar, current track metadata, and thumbnail.\n\n### Deliverables Required:\n- The full project structure and file tree.\n- `package.json` with required dependencies.\n- The NextAuth configuration file with the strict email check.\n- The `yt-dlp` API route handler.\n- Core TSX components (Layout, Sidebar, Dashboard, and Sticky Player)."
    }
  }
}
