  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Backend Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on planning the backend architecture. My recent thought process revolves around the design of the yt-dlp executable and stream extraction service. I\'m exploring the file location, and am considering the server start procedure for checking the yt-dlp file.\n\n\n**Implementing yt-dlp Integration**\n\nI\'ve made progress in integrating yt-dlp. I\'ve defined functions for track information extraction and searching using the executable. Specifically, `extractTrackInfo` handles both URL and query searches, returning track metadata. The `searchTracks` function handles querying for specific tracks, with a configurable result count. Now, I\'m working on the audio stream proxy to resolve direct audio stream URLs.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Audio Streaming**\n\nI\'m now focusing on audio streaming. I\'m exploring two methods: piping audio directly using `yt-dlp` for efficient browser `<audio>` seeking, and using an HTTP proxy to support range requests and ensure smooth streaming, avoiding CORS and header issues. My goal is seamless audio playback.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m presently focused on establishing data structures. I\'ve defined interfaces for `Track`, `Playlist`, and `LibraryData`, including properties like duration, addedAt, and track IDs. My goal is to use these interfaces for database management, and I am considering implementing thread-safe read/write operations for data access via `fs.readFileSync` and `fs.writeFileSync`.\n\n\n**Designing API Authentication**\n\nI\'m now deep into designing the API authentication routes. I\'ve defined `google-login`, `quick-auth`, `logout`, and session management endpoints. The `quick-auth` is especially interesting as it simplifies testing. I\'ve also incorporated session cookies for enhanced security and streamlined access.\n\n\n**Defining API Routes**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out API routes, and defined several endpoints. I\'m implementing PUT, DELETE, and POST methods to handle playlist updates, deletions, and track history. GET requests now include search functionality via yt-dlp, and track resolution. I\'ve also established a direct audio stream endpoint for efficient music playback.\n\n**Structuring Frontend Components**\n\nI\'m structuring the frontend and defining component relationships. Within `src/`, I\'ve established core types in `src/types.ts` for data interfaces. I\'ve built the AuthContext to handle single-user authentication and implemented a PlayerContext to orchestrate YouTube Music audio playback with the `<audio>` element events. I\'m focusing on defining component relationships.\n\n\n**Defining Player Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the player\'s functionality and its UI components. I\'ve designed the `PlayerContext` to manage audio playback states: `currentTime`, `duration`, and `volume`, along with controls like `isMuted`, `isShuffle`, `repeatMode`, and `isLoadingStream`. I am implementing functions to manipulate track playback and to manage the current and future tracks. I\'m structuring three key components: `Sidebar`, `Header`, and `PlayerBar` which make use of these functions and states.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Player Controls**\n\nI am now implementing the user interface for player controls. I\'ve focused on the play/pause, next track, and repeat functionality. I\'ve designed a seek bar with elapsed and total duration displays, an interactive slider, and a visual buffer bar. I\'m also implementing a queue drawer toggle, a volume control with a mute toggle and slider, and a full-screen/expanded visualizer player modal. I\'m thinking about how each button can interact with the underlying PlayerContext.\n\n\n**Constructing Frontend Views**\n\nI\'m now building out frontend views. I\'m designing the `PlaylistDetailView.tsx` with a playlist hero, reorderable track list, and edit controls. The `SearchView.tsx` will have instant YouTube search results. I\'m also planning the `AddTrackModal.tsx` for easy track addition and a sleek `UnauthorizedScreen.tsx` for restricted users.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 347969530
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
